# Stripe Connect Express — Clean Connect

> Activé sur `apps/api/src/modules/payments/**`.
> Cahier des charges : §4.3 et §4.4.
> ADRs : [ADR-008 Escrow capture_method=manual + delayed transfer](../../docs/adr/ADR-008-escrow-manual-capture-delayed-transfer.md), [ADR-011 Stripe API pinning](../../docs/adr/ADR-011-stripe-api-pinning.md).

---

## Flow paiement complet — `capture_method='manual'` + delayed transfer (ADR-008)

```
1. Client paie une mission (avant publication, cf. D15 + Q4)
   → PaymentIntent créé avec capture_method='manual' (autorisation, pas de débit)
   → automatic_payment_methods.enabled=true (3DS automatique, Q8)
   → idempotencyKey serveur déterministe = 'pi-mission-{missionId}-{attempt}'
   → application_fee_amount calculé serveur (18 % HT, jamais transmis client)
   → Pas de transfer_data.destination (transfer différé via stripe.transfers.create après capture)
   → Webhook payment_intent.amount_capturable_updated → PaymentStatus.AUTHORIZED
   → Mission: PENDING_PAYMENT → PAID → PUBLISHED (visible matching)

2. Prestataire accepte + exécute la mission
   → Mission: ACCEPTED → IN_PROGRESS (≥ 3 BEFORE syncées) → CLIENT_VALIDATION_PENDING (≥ 5 AFTER syncées)
   → BullMQ delayed job 'escrow.auto-release' programmé à T+48h ouvrées (jobId 'auto-release-{missionId}')
   → Rappels push + email programmés à T+24h, T+36h, T+47h ouvrées (ADR-012 + ADR-013)
   → AutoReleaseJob.status = SCHEDULED

3a. Client valide manuellement (POST /missions/:id/validate)
    → Job BullMQ enqueue : capture + transfer (jamais synchrone HTTP)
    → stripe.paymentIntents.capture(piId, { idempotencyKey: 'capture-mission-{missionId}' })
    → Webhook payment_intent.succeeded → PaymentStatus.CAPTURED
    → stripe.transfers.create({ destination, amount: providerPayoutCents, source_transaction }, { idempotencyKey: 'transfer-mission-{missionId}' })
    → Webhook transfer.paid → TransferStatus.SENT
    → Mission: COMPLETED, AutoReleaseJob.status = CANCELLED (cancelReason='client_validated')

3b. Pas de réponse à T+48h ouvrées
    → Job 'escrow.auto-release' s'exécute (lock applicatif AutoReleaseJob.lockedAt/lockedBy)
    → canReleaseEscrow() vérifie photos BEFORE/AFTER + pas de dispute + payoutStatus READY + PaymentStatus AUTHORIZED encore valide
    → Si OK : capture + transfer idempotents (mêmes clés que 3a)
    → AutoReleaseJob.status = COMPLETED, Mission: AUTO_RELEASED → COMPLETED

3c. Client conteste (POST /missions/:id/report-problem, fenêtre limitée)
    → Mission: → DISPUTE_OPEN, audit DISPUTE_OPENED
    → Job 'escrow.auto-release' annulé via lock + cancelReason='dispute_opened'
    → AutoReleaseJob.status = CANCELLED
    → Process litige (modules/disputes/) — vrai workflow PRD-005

3d. Authorization Stripe expirée (>7j Visa/MC sans capture)
    → stripe.paymentIntents.capture() renvoie 'authorization_expired'
    → Audit CAPTURE_FAILED, AutoReleaseJob.status = FAILED + DLQ + alerte ops
    → Mission reste CLIENT_VALIDATION_PENDING (retry manuel admin)
    → POST /missions/:id/validate côté client → 409 PAYMENT_AUTHORIZATION_EXPIRED

3e. Refund admin (POST /payments/:id/refund — intégral uniquement MVP)
    → Refund.status = PENDING, PaymentStatus.REFUND_PENDING
    → stripe.refunds.create({ payment_intent, amount, reason }, { idempotencyKey: 'refund-mission-{missionId}-{attempt}' })
    → Webhook charge.refunded → Refund.status = REFUNDED, PaymentStatus.REFUNDED
    → Échec : Refund.status = FAILED, PaymentStatus rollback à CAPTURED, retry admin via nouvel Idempotency-Key
```

**Interdit** :
- `transfer_data.destination` au PaymentIntent (Destination charges refusé — Q1).
- Capture synchrone côté handler HTTP (toujours queue BullMQ retryable — D9).
- Capture sans `idempotencyKey` (D14 + D18).
- Refund partiel MVP (`PAYMENT_PARTIAL_REFUND_NOT_SUPPORTED` 422).

